Legend: LS_impr% = share of particle-evals where local search improved the decoded plan;
desyncKT = normalised Kendall distance between the keys' own permutation (what pbest stores) and the LS-improved plan that earned the stored cost;
nat_chg% = share of native (pre-tunnel) updates that change the decoded permutation at all; nat_KT = mean Kendall change of native update;
rho = Spearman corr between key-space distance moved and Kendall change; total_KT = mean Kendall change incl. tunneling;
mbStd = std of mbest across customers (0 => flat vector), early/late; mbDev = mean |mbest - x|.
